  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0210 database is a library management system that stores information about authors, genres, books, members, librarians, transactions, and book reviews. The authors table contains information about the authors of books, including their names, birth dates, nationalities, and biographies. The genres table contains information about the genres of books, including their names and descriptions. The books table contains information about the books themselves, including their titles, authors, genres, publication dates, ISBNs, available and total copies, and descriptions. The members table contains information about the members of the library, including their names, enrollment dates, emails, phone numbers, addresses, and descriptions. The borrow table contains information about the books that members have borrowed, including the book IDs, member IDs, borrow dates, due dates, and return dates. The librarians table contains information about the librarians who work at the library, including their names, emails, phone numbers, addresses, and descriptions. The transactions table contains information about the transactions that have taken place in the library, including the book IDs, member IDs, librarian IDs, transaction dates, transaction types, and descriptions. The book_reviews table contains information about the reviews that members have left for books, including the book IDs, member IDs, ratings, comments, and review dates.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context  \nThe project involves developing a library management system using the `LibraryCatalog` database. This system is designed to organize and manage information related to books, patrons, loans, and returns in a library environment.\n\n2) Objectives  \nThe primary objective is to facilitate efficient management of library resources, ensuring that books can be easily tracked and managed. This includes handling book inventories, managing patron information, overseeing borrowing and returning processes, and recording transactions.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Stakeholders: Library administrators, head librarians, and IT department.\n- Users: Patrons (members), librarians, and possibly support staff for data entry.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- Books Management: Maintain records of books, including title, author, genre, publication date, and availability.\n- Authors and Genres: Manage and categorize books using author and genre information.\n- Patron Management: Keep detailed records of library members, including personal information and membership details.\n- Loan Management: Track borrowing activities with details such as the borrow date, due date, and return date.\n- Review System: Allow members to review and rate books they have read.\n- Transactions: Log all transactions involving book borrowings, returns, and other library operations with involvement from both members and librarians.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- Performance: The system should handle multiple transactions and queries concurrently without significant delay.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for both members and librarians to perform library operations efficiently.\n- Scalability: Be capable of handling an increasing number of books and members as the library grows.\n- Security: Ensure the protection of member information and transaction data from unauthorized access.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0210.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0210\nCREATE TABLE `authors` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `genres` (\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`genre_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `books` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `genre_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `available_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_copies` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `authors` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `books_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`genre_id`) REFERENCES `genres` (`genre_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `members` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `enrollment_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `librarians` (\n  `librarian_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`librarian_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `borrow` (\n  `borrow_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `due_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`borrow_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `borrow_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `borrow_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transactions` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `librarian_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`librarian_id`) REFERENCES `librarians` (`librarian_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_reviews` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_reviews_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `books` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_reviews_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `members` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
